course: dictionary
lesson: 5176
title: The Israelites
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An Israelite was a member of the ancient people of Israel. Their stories are told in the Hebrew Bible, which Christians call the Old Testament. «The Israelites in Egypt» means the Israelites who lived in Egypt at that time.
explain: Israelite can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun it names people: «Moses led the Israelites out of Egypt.» As an adjective it describes things that belong to that people, such as Israelite history.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «God parted the sea so the Israelites crossed on dry ground» tells you the Israelites were people in a story about escape. Jews today see the Israelites as their ancestors.
fact: An Israelite is a member of the ancient people of Israel.
fact: The Israelites were the descendants of Jacob.
fact: «The Israelites wandered forty years in the wilderness» before reaching the Promised Land.
fact: «Ruth was not an Israelite, yet she was welcomed and became the great-grandmother of King David.»
fact: Israelite can be a noun (an Israelite, Israelites) or an adjective (Israelite).
exercise: In «God parted the sea so the Israelites crossed on dry ground», who crossed on dry ground? | *The Israelites | Moses alone | Ruth | Pharaoh's army
exercise: What does Israelite mean? | A kind of sea | A king of Egypt | *A member of the ancient people of Israel | A member of a modern town council
exercise: Which phrase uses Israelite to describe a thing? | Ruth was an Israelite | *Israelite history | Israelites crossed the sea | The Israelites left Egypt
test: In «The Israelites wandered forty years in the wilderness», where did they wander? | Their homes in Egypt | In King David's palace | *In the wilderness | At the Red Sea
test: Where did God give the Ten Commandments? | At the Red Sea | *At Mount Sinai | In Egypt | In the Promised Land
exam: Who led the Israelites out of Egypt? | King David | Joseph | *Moses | Ruth
